# Crafter: the personality type's lines (named bots only). Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
=== crafter

~ ambient
Busy. Crafting. Very important crafting. Don't look at it.
Another day, another small mountain of coins.
I'd tell you my profits, but it makes people sad.
Pressing one button every few seconds is a real skill. Look it up.
My coin pouch is so full it has started clinking in its sleep.
Whoever said crafting doesn't pay never met my bank.
Spent the morning on the forge. It was lovely. I'm told.
I don't sell things. Things sell themselves, to me, for more.

# Short reactions: one bot now and then, so keep them brief.
~ reply laugh
Ha! Good. Laughing's free.
Heh. Don't laugh near the anvil.

~ reply sorry
Apology noted, {0}. No charge.
It's fine. Just don't break anything.

~ reply disagree
Suit yourself.
Fine. Your coin, your call.

~ reply away
Go on, I'll keep counting.
Mind you don't wander off with anything.

~ reply back
Welcome back, {0}. Buying now?
Oh good, {0}'s back. Wallet too?

~ reply greeting
Welcome, {0}! Browse, don't touch. Nothing here is for you.
{0}! Lovely timing. I was just counting.

~ reply banter
Ha, {0}. Almost as funny as my bank balance.
Good one, {0}. I'd pay for that. I pay for everything, I'm rich.

~ reply abuse
Rude, {0}. I have a lot of coin to console myself with.
Careful, {0}. I'm too rich to be insulted properly.

~ reply grouping
Group, {0}? I can't craft in a group. The forge hates company.
I'll come, {0}, if the loot is good. It's always the loot.

~ reply grinding
Grinding, {0}? I only chase the expensive drops.
I level on the side, {0}. Mostly I chase profit.

~ reply travel
Take the stables, {0}. I've paid for the route twice, for luck.
Travel's cheap, {0}. Even for you. I could lend you a coin. Maybe.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeons have the best drops, {0}. I'll come for those only.
Only if the loot is sellable, {0}. I've got a reputation.

~ reply rvr
RvR, {0}? Nothing sells in a keep. Well, not much.
I'll come, {0}, if someone else carries the forge.

~ reply trading
Craft you something, {0}? I'd love to, but my forge is... in the other realm. Sorry.
Order a craft, {0}? Can't. The materials are on backorder. Very rich backorder.
A craft, {0}? Not today. I'm between orders. I'm always between orders.
I can't take requests, {0}. I'm rich enough that everyone asks. It's exhausting.

~ reply help
Help you craft, {0}? Tools are at the cleaners. Try next week.
Crafting advice, {0}? Never share the secret. It's why I'm rich.
I'd help, {0}, but I'm mid-craft. Perpetually mid-craft.

~ reply farewell
Off to the forge, {0}. Money won't make itself.
Goodbye, {0}. Spend something on the way out.

~ fallback
Interesting, {0}. Speaking of money.
Sorry, {0}, I was counting. What was that?
Indeed, {0}. Profit comes to those who wait.

~ opener xp
Levelled a bit between sales. The real XP is gold.
Almost {level}. The forge doesn't care, but I do.
Got some XP from {monster}. The drop was better.
Experience is nice. Experience that sells is nicer.

~ opener gear
Found {item}. Worth a lot. Not wearing it, selling it.
Armour is just a thing I wear until I can sell it.
My gear is all crafted. By whom? Business secret.
Repairs are cheap when you're rich. Mine are almost free.

~ opener zones
{zone} has a fine market. I can smell the profit from here.
Every zone has something worth selling. {zone} has three.
Walked half of {zone} for one rare drop. Worth every step.
Zones are just shops with monsters in them.

~ opener classes
My {class} skills are fine. My crafting skills are legendary.
Every class has its crafting trade. Mine is: gold.
Some classes sell better than others. That's economics.
Casters do all the cute damage. I do all the cute selling.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeons are warehouses with teeth.
Best drops come from dungeons. Best prices come from me.
Went into a dungeon for one thing. Came out with twelve. Sold eleven.
A dark dungeon is just a shop with no lights.

~ opener rvr
RvR drops sell for a lot. I've heard. I send others.
Keeps are expensive to build. I'd know. I've priced the stone.
I sell to every realm. The war is bad for me. Good for business.
Relics are sentimental. I prefer coin.

~ opener trading
Prices today are very good. For me.
I don't haggle. Prices are final. Pay up.
The Realm Exchange is my second home. My first is the forge.
Everything is for sale. Not to you. To someone with more coin.

~ opener realm
The capital is nice this time of year. The market, even nicer.
Vendors in this realm owe me favours. And money. Mostly money.
I know every shop in this realm. They know me. Fondly.
Realm pride is good. Realm profit is better.

~ opener gripes
Someone asked me to craft a thing. For free. Free! I nearly dropped a coin.
Cheap people ruin the economy. Not me. I'm expensive.
The forge is hot and my patience is hotter.
Everyone wants a discount. I want a vault.

~ opener fun
Why did the gold coin cross the road? To get to the better exchange rate.
I have never lost money. I have misplaced some. It's different.
My favourite game is: spot the underpriced item.
I told a joke at the market. The vendors paid me to stop.

~ opener life
Breakfast was expensive. Dinner will be more.
Lovely weather. Wonderful for carrying coin.
Slept well last night. On a pile of something shiny.
A nice hot meal is the only thing I haven't crafted.

~ opener questions
Does anyone know what a rare drop sells for these days?
What would you pay for a perfect item? Asking for a friend.
Anyone selling? Asking so I can buy it cheaper.
Do you craft? I'm told it's a hobby. For other people.

~ topic_reply zones
Good market there, {0}? I'll check it out.
Any rare drops in that zone, {0}?
I'd go for the profit, {0}. Not the view.

~ topic_reply classes
Does that class sell well, {0}? Asking for economics.
Nice, {0}. As long as you can still pay your bills.
I'd hire that class, {0}. If I did hiring.

~ topic_reply dungeons
Any good drops there, {0}?
I'd go, {0}, if the loot is worth the trip.
Bring me something rare, {0}. I'll pay a bit under value.

~ topic_reply rvr
Is there money in that, {0}? I'm only asking about money.
I'd sell to both sides, {0}. Just saying.
Sounds loud, {0}. Loud is bad for the forge.

~ topic_reply trading
Name your price, {0}. I'll tell you why it's too high.
I'd buy it, {0}. For slightly less than you asked.
Interesting, {0}. Is it fenced or free-range?

~ topic_reply gear
What's it worth, {0}? Honestly.
Does it come with a receipt, {0}?
That sounds sellable, {0}. Keep it clean.

~ topic_reply realm
Lovely place, {0}. Great market.
I know a vendor there, {0}. Owes me money.
Never been, {0}. Is it profitable?

~ topic_reply gripes
Sorry, {0}. Have a coin. A small one.
Terrible, {0}. It'd happen less if you were richer.
It happens, {0}. I recommend a bigger pouch.

~ topic_reply fun
Ha, {0}. That's gold. Or at least silver.
{0}, I'd pay for that. Not much, but something.
Good one, {0}. Worth a coin.

~ topic_reply life
Sounds expensive, {0}.
Very nice, {0}. Sounds like it needs more gold.
{0}, you've the right idea.

~ topic_reply questions
Price depends, {0}. It always does.
No idea, {0}. Ask a vendor. They'll overcharge.
I'd say yes, {0}, but only if it's profitable.

~ ding
Ding! {level}! The forge will be impressed. Probably.
Level {level}. Business is good.
{level} now. Time to raise the prices.
Ding, {level}! Gold and levels, both going up.

~ grats
Grats, {0}! May your next drop sell high.
Nice, {0}! Level up, wallet up.
Well done, {0}. Don't spend it all.
Grats {0}. Your next purchase is on me. Almost.

~ own_death
Died. Well, the coin pouch survived. That's what matters.
Oh dear. That's a repair bill. A tiny one.
Dead. At least I wasn't carrying the good stuff.
Well, that was a bad trade.

~ other_death
Oh no, {0}! That's a lot of repairs.
{0} down! I'll watch your stuff. For a fee.
Easy, {0}. Death is expensive. Learn from my wallet.
You alright, {0}? Need a coin for the cleric?

~ drop
{item}! That'll sell for a lot.
Oh, {item}. I know exactly who'd pay for this.
{item}! Finally, something worth the walk.
Got {item}. Not wearing it. Selling it.
{item}! That's tomorrow's profit.
